      "reason": "The pre-231-05 committed floor (33642 total open_findings, 197 light-desktop-populated / 181 dark-desktop-populated per non-proxy surface) was captured on renders that ABORTED before most probes ever ran: phase (a) of the admin-eval harness had never once completed in CI before this plan. Two blocking bugs (WebKit browser absence for admin-eval-mobile, and an SVGAnimatedString crash in probes.ts ember-class check) made every prior CI attempt fail partway through phase (a), so admin-render-sha.json reflected an incomplete render, not a genuine full CI-native measurement. 231-04 fixed both blocking bugs; this plan (231-05) additionally reconciled three probes against ratified-but-never-exercised design decisions (D-08 chip-remove control scale, pill/code padding sub-scale tokens, gallery-frame card nesting) and fixed a pre-existing gap in fix-queue-lint.sh (proxy-surface cross-surface exemption). With all of that landed, run 30509363963 is the first render in this repository history where phase (a) reached 192/192 (0 failed) and phase (a2)/(b1)/(b2) all executed and passed for the first time ever. 171 bundle.json files were downloaded from the admin-eval-bundles-30509363963 artifact and verified via a downloaded bundle.json to carry app_git_sha equal to 18c2720aa42d49073019f003603e54b53b161d7d, matching the run headSha and confirmed independently by the run own stale-render-guard (b1: PASS, 171 bundle(s) verified at HEAD). The new totals below are the CI-native output of node scripts/ci/fix-queue-build.mjs run against those 171 bundles, the same sole-writer program CI itself runs, not a hand-edited number. None of this plan changes could have caused an increase: the chip-remove fix, pill/code rescoping, and card-nesting suppression all strictly remove gate throws relative to what the harness would otherwise report.",
